# Grid B — U3 Comparison (A vs B across two files)
#
# Gap target: no comparison_table shape; complexity detects "对比"
# cue but still compiles to architecture_explain with a single
# narrative shape. This case measures symmetry — answer must cover
# BOTH sides in structurally equal depth, not lean to one file.
#
# EXPECT_SECTIONS is the main gate: both file names must appear.
# This is stricter than EXPECT_CONTAINS (which only checks that ALL
# needles appear) in intent — sections are semantic requirements, so
# summary.md shows "missing_section:X" rather than "missing:X" when
# symmetry is violated.
#
# Ground truth: explorer.go's ShouldStop consults LLM-provided
# completion signals plus heuristics (idle streak, iteration cap).
# extractor.go's ShouldStop is one-shot — it stops after the first
# emit_answer_symbol / emit_hypothesis_verdict call. Any correct
# answer will contrast "multi-round heuristic" vs "one-shot emit".
ID="u3a"
NAME="comparison — explorer vs extractor ShouldStop conditions"
QUESTION="对比 explorer.go 和 extractor.go 的 ReAct 循环终止条件有何不同？给出两个文件里 ShouldStop 方法的行为对比，逐条列出差异。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was just `ShouldStop` —
# the method name in the question; bar = "复述题目". The case
# already had EXPECT_SECTIONS for the two filenames (good), but
# nothing enforced the BEHAVIORAL difference enumeration the
# question demands. Strengthen by requiring answer to surface the
# core asymmetry: explorer is multi-round (iteration / completion
# / idle / heuristic), extractor is one-shot (first emit /
# emit_answer_symbol). Permits English or Chinese phrasing.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="ShouldStop"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(iteration|轮次|多轮|multi.?round|completion)
(one.?shot|first emit|首次|emit_answer_symbol|emit_hypothesis_verdict)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="identical same.behavior .java"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="explorer.go extractor.go"
